WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/telemetry/components/SignalStatsPanel.tsx — a PURE presentation-only wrapper around DataTable,
  fed `stats: SignalStat[]` ({signal,min,max,avg,count}) and an optional `selectedSignals` list by its parents
  (the telemetry Workspace + Explorer pages). Regions / behaviour:
    GlassPanel(p-4/5) → header: span.section-title ("Stats Summary" or a `title` override) + a "Hide empty (N)"
                        Toggle (size sm) shown ONLY when `emptyCount > 0` (local useState(false)).
                      → body: `loading ? <Skeleton h-20 ×4 grid>` : `visibleStats.length > 0 ? <DataTable
                        compact paginated>` : `<span>No stats available</span>`.
    displayStats      : when `selectedSignals` is provided, one row per selected signal — back-filling absent
                        signals with an em-dash row (NaN min/max/avg, count 0) carrying a "No data in range" hint;
                        otherwise `stats` verbatim.
    columns (5)       : Signal (mono name coloured `CHART_COLORS[max(0,idx)%len]`, "No data in range" subtitle when
                        empty) · Min · Max (mono, text-secondary, "—"+aria "No data" when non-finite) · Avg (mono,
                        text-primary, "—") · Count (mono, text-muted, fmtInt).
    visibleStats      : `hideEmpty ? displayStats.filter(!isEmptyStat) : displayStats`; emptyCount = #empty rows.
  Data sources: `useTranslation` only. No data hooks at the leaf; loading/error/stale/offline are owned by the
  parent surface that feeds `stats` — reproduced here as the P4 leaf contract. Formatting helpers it consumes:
  fmtNumber / fmtInt (numberFormat.ts, global precision 2, safeNumber⇒0).
  i18n keys extracted: signalStats.noDataInRange ("No data in range"), signalStats.hideEmpty ("Hide empty
  ({{count}})"), plus the bare t() column/title/empty strings (Signal/Min/Max/Avg/Count/Stats Summary/No stats
  available).

