PARITY MAP (semantic, ADR-006 — platform tokens, not Tailwind ports)
  per-signal name colour → TSChartPalette.color(at: max(0,idx)) over the brand categorical palette (= web
                           CHART_COLORS index mapping, wrapping + negative-safe)
  min/max cells          → Color.TS.textSecondary ; avg → Color.TS.textPrimary ; count → Color.TS.textMuted
  fmtNumber/fmtInt       → SignalStatsFormat.number/int (2-decimal vs 0-decimal, half-away, safeNumber⇒0, locale)
  renderNumeric "—"      → SignalStatsFormat.numeric (non-finite ⇒ em-dash) + a11y "No data"
  Toggle size="sm"       → SwiftUI Toggle .toggleStyle(.switch) .controlSize(.small) .tint(Color.TS.accent)
  i18n      : every web string via the P1/S10 facade (SignalStatsStrings, table "SignalStatsPanel"); zero English
              literals in code. The hide-empty count is interpolated via String(format:) %lld.
  a11y      : each row carries a combined VoiceOver label ("{signal}, Min …, Max …, Avg …, Count …" or
              "{signal}, No data in range"); em-dash cells labelled "No data"; loading grid labelled; the header is
              an .isHeader; Dynamic Type + Reduce Motion respected via the shared tokens/components.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="SignalStatsPanel" via SignalStatsModel.start (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.
  states    : loading (skeleton grid) / empty (web "No stats available" → ContentUnavailableView) / error (parent
              query failure, retry) / data, plus the P4 leaf freshness axis live / stale (chip+banner+one-shot
              auto-refresh) / offline (chip+banner). The hide-empty-filters-everything sub-case re-uses the web
              "No stats available" text.

